{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>למכה</b> — 'and slew' — the meaning is doubled, and now he specified them because they were mighty. And so the prophet said concerning the Amorite: 'whose height was like the height of cedars and who was strong like oaks'; and likewise: 'I delivered the Amorite by my sword and by my bow, for the iniquity of the Amorite was not yet complete.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 136, :notes {0 "The verse citations appear to amalgamate Amos 2:9 and Genesis 15:16 with an allusion to prophetic language; rendered as Ibn Ezra quotes them."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:54.440915597Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}